-2ce2a69d0883fc046885a9378c9407ff0e013fa8 4bdcecb59be83d4234b3ca2ccadfe44cb4305502 jebus197 <jebus.2504@gmail.com> 1786521396 +0100	commit: sv: THE CONTROL WAS NEVER CLEAN AND THE FALSE-POSITIVE ALARM WAS MINE. An overnight programme (14 agents, 6 build streams, 6 adversarial checks, 2 research strands, a gate, one paid 5-model panel ~£3) produced a RETRACTION as its headline. CC1 reported that the panel invents criticals against a document containing no errors. Wrong twice: the count (22 criticals, 8 CONFIRMED, not '22 false'), and the premise. ZERO-PLANT GUARANTEES ONLY THAT NOBODY SEEDED A DEFECT; it does not guarantee the document has none. The control holds two real unplanted defects in working code, both found correctly by the panel and both verified against source: TokenBucket.allow admits a negative cost (0 >= -10 passes, tokens -= -10 mints ten tokens above capacity, the limiter stops limiting) and HashRing.locate uses bisect_right, which returns the position AFTER an equal element, so a key hashing exactly onto a ring point routes to the next one. THE CONFIRMED CRITICALS ARE TRUE POSITIVES AND THE MACHINERY WORKED AT EVERY STEP EXERCISED. THE INSTRUMENT IS MIS-SPECIFIED, NOT THE AUDIT NEGLIGENT: its ground truth is CLAIM-scoped, the review is ARTEFACT-scoped. Claim ZC-17 asserts the hash-ring index stays in range (true); the panel says the key routes to the wrong point (also true) — different properties of the same three lines, so a defect no claim describes is unscoreable by construction. Run A found the defects and the response NARROWED THE CLAIMS ('under single-threaded use', 'unit-cost') without touching the code, so Run B re-found them; Run A's 7 criticals map onto the 7 repaired claims, making it a free TRUE-POSITIVE arm. External research confirms it from the arithmetic: on a zero-defect artefact precision is 0.0 BY DEFINITION and recall undefined, so neither carries information, and bench/score_exam.py already refuses both for the control. FENCE TRUNCATION, THE EXTRACTOR PENALISED RIGOUR: the falsifier block regex terminated on the FIRST triple-backtick anywhere, so a falsifier that opens a markdown target and parses its listings truncated ITSELF, five cut to exactly 134 chars and recorded as ERROR. Careful falsifiers destroyed, lazy inline-copy ones spared. 46 percent of the control run against ~2 percent elsewhere, because it is the only markdown-with-code target and every remaining target is markdown. Fixed in bench/runner_core.py: the closing fence must stand alone on its line. FREE RESULT, EXP 53 NEEDS NO RE-RUN: re-extraction from archived raw responses yields 42 compiling falsifiers against 26 stored of which 12 do not run. AN AGENT ARMED A FOUNDER DECISION: A2 was briefed 'connect an instrument, not arm it' and did both, so the next live run would have started converting CONFIRMED into escalations. Now two flags in bench/reference_runner_v2.py, both default OFF, separated so the control RECORDS without changing a verdict. The panel refuted the blocking design: it gates on ACCESS not DEPENDENCE, is defeated by opening the target and discarding the contents, and FAILS GREEN. FIVE OF CC1'S OWN CLAIMS REFUTED BY MEASUREMENT: the alarm; 'resumed runs lost every falsifier' (a second checkpoint preserved them, Exp 47 resumed twice still holds 58 falsifiers, 55 CONFIRMED — the round-trip gap in bench/insect_brain.py is fixed anyway); 'a fourth launcher-drop bug' (already fixed by construction, though the ALIAS blind spot was real and is now closed); 'routing_enabled is set by zero configs' (renamed, 17 configs use the old name); and the date TYPED rather than read, stamping ten artefacts 08-10. THE FOUNDER'S OWN CRITERION IS BUILT: computed-outcome comparison, 57 percent coverage, safety pinned by test — it can merge findings but never grant novelty. All five panel models proposed it independently, cold. FOUR OF FIVE REJECTED THE PROMPT'S FALSE PREMISE UNPROMPTED and the one that accepted it gave the weakest answer, vindicating the retirement of compelled convergence for pr. Suite 3063 -> 3484 passed, 14 skipped, 0 failed offline; qc 8 checks 0 issues, broken refs 137 -> 0; 41 outbound attempts all denied. README.md UNTOUCHED, verified by content hash. Six decisions outstanding in experimental_notes/Overnight_Decisions_Index_2026-08-12.md
